       pod/buildtoc - Generate table of contents

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program generates a table of contents for the documentation
       included in the Perl core distribution.  This table of contents takes
       two forms:

       1 _p_o_d_/_p_e_r_l_t_o_c_._p_o_d
           A file in Perl's Plain Old Documentation (POD) format found in the
           _p_o_d_/ directory in the core distribution.  Once Perl is installed,
           this file becomes accessible system-wide via "perldoc perltoc".

       2 _p_o_d_/_r_o_f_f_i_t_a_l_l
           A shell script originally written by Tom Christiansen and Raphael
           Manfredi, also found in the _p_o_d_/ directory, which can be used to
           translate Perl documentation into _m_a_n pages.

UUSSAAGGEE
       This program will typically nnoott need to be called directly by a user.
       Rather, it is one of the last commands invoked during "make test_prep":

           ./perl -Ilib -I. -f pod/buildtoc -q

       The only command-line switch is "-q|--quiet", which quiets some non-
       critical warnings.

